\tag{fdip}
\title{Coarse quantum observations and temporal memory}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{Observe only the first coordinate of the coupled quartic chain in \ref{fdip-00GV}.
Its positive vacuum in \ref{fdip-00H6} gives an exact probability law for that
coordinate, while the Hamiltonian still evolves the entire chain. What information
determines the retained observations at several times?}

\p{Measurable observations include selected sites, spatial averages and nonlinear
functions of a configuration. The finite-volume vacuum and Euclidean correlations
of [[fdip-00H1]] give their joint laws. For orthogonal selectors of finite
Gaussian-reference data, exact integration in \ref{fdip-00GI} supplies retained
densities.}

